"Never define a React component inside another component's render body -- hoist it to module scope and pass props. A nested definition is a brand-new component type on every parent render, so React unmounts and remounts its whole subtree each time: scroll positions reset, animations restart, local element state is lost. Deliberate element replacement is expressed the opposite way: a stable identity key (entity id) that CHANGES only when the subject genuinely changes (new room, new focus), never as a side effect of re-rendering."